{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd.pop('experiment',None)\nd['repeat_experiment_id']='cff2222705354f669ca24cef6629804a-experiment'\nd['rationale']=d['rationale']+\\\" Reproducibility question: the corrected resurrected-voter experiment is repeated once from its retained inputs in a clean copy, because the premature-commit observation depends on the stale leader winning its re-election after the restart and on the removed voter having caught up before the partition.\\\"\n# child interpretation -> established\nchild=d['interpretations'][1]\nchild['experiment_id']='cff2222705354f669ca24cef6629804a-experiment'\nchild['conclusion']='violated'\nchild['defect_claim']='asserted'\nchild['executions']={'226f9762f0b444f69c154b35fe0788f3':[1,3],'ee57ec0448704270bcbc1cf7ace9a045':[1]}\nchild['rationale']=(\\\"Two retained receipts. ee57ec0448704270bcbc1cf7ace9a045 established the membership half (restarted leader lists the removed voter C: three servers and two peers against B's two servers and one peer) but did not reach the write observation because B won the post-restart election. The corrected harness 226f9762f0b444f69c154b35fe0788f3 scores all four comparisons as predicted: the resurrected membership (violated, witness index 1), the control keeping two servers (holds, index 5), the premature commit (violated, witness index 3: write_applied=true, entry_index 10, A commit and applied index 10, B's log still at 9, entry_on_quorum=false), and the control refusing the same write under the committed membership (holds, index 7, 'leadership lost while committing log'). Source: with Servers still containing C, the commitment installed on append (raft.go 1236-1241) makes A+C a quorum of the stale {A,B,C}, while the configuration committed in the log is {A,B} (quorum 2, both members), and the leader applies what it believes committed.\\\")\nchild['counterevidence']=[\\\"The control mode shows the same cluster, partition and stores refusing the write ('leadership lost while committing log') when the leader's configuration is the committed one, so the premature commit is attributable to the stale membership and not to the partition alone.\\\"]\nchild['limitations']=[\\\"The partition is an explicit transport disconnection between A and B; the removed voter C is up and caught up, which is required for A to see a quorum in its stale view.\\\",\\\"A repeat of this experiment is requested in this update because the observation depends on the stale leader winning its re-election and on C's catch-up completing before the partition.\\\"]\n# parent limitation refresh\npar=d['interpretations'][0]\npar['limitations']=[l for l in par['limitations'] if 'child question\\\\'s retained receipt' not in l]\npar['limitations'] += [\n \\\"The child question is now established by retained receipt 226f9762f0b444f69c154b35fe0788f3 (resurrected membership and a write applied on the leader with B, required by the committed configuration, never receiving the entry; control refuses the same write), so the parents' consequence list includes premature commitment under a stale membership.\\\"]\nd['knowledge']=d.get('knowledge',[])+[{\n \\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":\\\"A stale in-memory configuration drives every membership decision of the node: configurationChangeChIfStable admits a configuration change once the stale latest and committed indexes look equal, appendConfigurationEntry derives the next membership from the stale base, commitment is installed from that new configuration on append, and both the election quorum and checkLeaderLease use the latest in-memory configuration. After a restart with RestoreCommittedLogs a node can therefore drop a voter that is only in its log, resurrect a voter whose removal is committed, and count a quorum of the stale membership: it commits and applies entries that a member required by the committed configuration has not accepted, and with a partitioned old voter it can truncate an entry it had committed.\\\",\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"RestoreCommittedLogs=true with a CommitTrackingLogStore and a log whose newest configuration entry lies inside the replayed committed prefix without a covering snapshot; the affected node must lead (or be elected) for the commitment, lease and configuration-change consequences.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"append_config_entry\\\",\\\"next_configuration\\\",\\\"commit_config_on_append\\\",\\\"truncate_conflict\\\",\\\"cfg_change_gate\\\",\\\"vote_prevote_checks\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"226f9762f0b444f69c154b35fe0788f3\\\":[1,3],\\\"6f9feceeefb245c288a7fd1f4497b83c\\\":[2,3,4]}}]\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
